00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.840
So as many of you may know,

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.260
the Early Childhood Peace
Consortium seeks to engage members

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.590
of the community here at
the Yale Child Study Center,

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.290
as well as the larger
Yale community and beyond

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.060
to explore the evidence,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.160
how we raise our children can be a pathway

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.680
to a more peaceful world.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.360
And for the last two decades,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.000
members of the Early
Childhood Peace Consortium

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.590
that work together with other members

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.390
of the international community,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.700
many of whom are actually
with us this morning

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.400
or this afternoon, depending on what area

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.960
of the world you live in,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:19.410
and we are continuing to make the effort

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.330
to establish a global movement

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.300
to build a more peaceful environment.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.290
And another member has
just arrived, so thank you.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.690
Thank you for being
downstairs. I appreciate it.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.360
So the goal of the Early
Childhood Peace Consortium is

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.570
to create a legacy of
sustained peace by drawing

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.140
on the transformative power
of early child development.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.570
And the global community
must address the root causes

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.610
of violence and conflict
so that the children

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.760
and families can be agents
of change for peace.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.330
And I guess I'd want to emphasize
the fact that we also need

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.240
to very much engage the
children and the young people

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.370
because they are the next generation

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.380
and it's gonna matter a lot in terms

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.883
of their perspective, as well.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.900
So our first presenter is dear Rima Salah,

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.830
who I've known for decades
and she's the current chair

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.690
of the Early Childhood Peace Consortium

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:16.110
and she has had all
sorts of important roles

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.480
at the United Nations and at UNICEF,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.430
really working in a number of countries

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.560
throughout Africa and other places.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.830
But she's also been a member
of our volunteer faculty here

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.000
at the Child Study Center,

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.030
and it's wonderful that she's here

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:31.393
for us more than a decade.

00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:35.280
So I think the floor is yours. Rima.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.830
- Yes. Thank you, thank you, Jim.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.160
Distinguished participants,
dear colleagues,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.890
it gives me a great pleasure to be

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.710
with you this morning, this afternoon,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.050
or this evening at the launch

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.417
of the new hybrid lecture series,

00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:56.730
"Raising Children of Peace" at
the Yale Chart Study Center,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.900
sponsored by the Early
Childhood Peace Consortium.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.340
I am privileged to have the
opportunity to talk to you

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.020
on a subject that concerns
us all in these very critical

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.070
and trying times,
building a world of peace,

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:18.363
the promise of the Early
Childhood Peace Consortium.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.680
Today, millions of children are trapped

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.950
in situations of war, conflict,

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:30.120
displacement and military occupation.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.710
For example, according to
Save the Children report 2021,

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:41.180
approximately 1.6 billion
children were living

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.700
in a conflict affected country.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.410
Approximately 449 million children,

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:54.410
over one in six were living
less than five kilometers

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.380
from where the active fighting took place.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.980
Some 230 million children lived

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.310
in high intensity conflict countries,

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:10.310
this exposing them to
killing, maiming, violence,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:14.520
abduction, separation from their families,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.020
and denial of humanitarian assistance,

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.020
leading to an unprecedented
crisis of care and learning.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.960
Yes, it is the story of lost childhood.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.860
What is alarming

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:36.600
and should concern us all is
the lasting negative impact

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.120
of deprivation and violence,

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.960
both physical and
structural on young children

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.683
and the detrimental effect
on children's development.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:52.470
Exposure to violence at an
early age is causally related

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:57.470
to a broad range of negative
outcomes across the lifespan,

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:03.110
including major emotional
and behavioral problems

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:07.320
which can be self-perpetuating,

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.440
and evidence-based science continues

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:14.543
to substantiate the link
between the early years of life

00:05:14.543 --> 00:05:19.543
and the early life environment
with long-term wellbeing.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.653
It also substantiates the link
between violent prevention

00:05:24.653 --> 00:05:29.490
and the development of
pro-social behavior that can lead

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.120
to more peaceful communities.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.290
Based also on the medical
journal, The Lancet, in 2016,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:41.730
it is clear that the
formative years of life

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.070
and and intra- and inter-family

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:48.240
and community relationships
are powerful agents

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.110
of change that can promote resilience,

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.173
social cohesion and peace.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:06:00.240
Distinguished participants,
the good news and hope is

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:03.990
that the emerging science
heralds a new era,

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:08.490
with windows of opportunities
through the investment

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.370
in the positive early
childhood development

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:16.370
of young children as a path,
creating a culture of peace,

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.470
sustaining peace at home in
the community and in a society

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:27.470
as a part of social transformation
and violence prevention.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:32.190
Distinguished participants,
the United Nations

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:36.847
and the international community
also heralds also a new era,

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:41.760
a new vision for building
peaceful societies,

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:45.510
an era where people are
at the center of peace

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.460
and development effort,

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:52.140
an era of inclusion with
all members of society,

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:57.140
including families and children
in the service of peace.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:01.560
The vision was captured by
the United Nations Agenda

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.440
for Sustainable Development Goals.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:09.440
And you know, at the heart
of the agenda is Goal 16,

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:14.750
which advocates to promote
peaceful and inclusive societies

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.710
for sustainable development
and provides access to justice

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.980
for all and build effective,

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.813
accountable and inclusive
institutions at all levels,

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.950
the adoption of the
agenda was a particularly,

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.740
historical moment for children,

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:38.340
especially the younger
ones and their parents.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:40.680
The agenda, for the first time,

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.910
includes early childhood development (ECD)

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:48.300
and recognized that
it's essential not just

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.300
for human development, but also
for sustainable development.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.150
The Secretary General
of the United Nations,

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:01.027
His Excellency Antonio Guterres said,

00:08:01.027 --> 00:08:05.610
"Violence against children
is widespread and pervasive,

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:07.800
but is not inevitable.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.800
By placing children at the
heart of the 2030 Agenda

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:16.380
and at the center of all what we do,

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:20.230
we can realize its novel
vision of a world free

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:26.280
from fear, a world free
from violence for all."

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.770
End of quotation.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:33.770
Distinguished participants,
to raise the voice of science,

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:39.260
to join the voice of "we the
people" in this new era for peace

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:45.860
that promotes the participation
of all members of society

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.800
in peace building efforts, as such,

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.800
calling for innovative and
transformative approaches

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.570
that engage family, parents,

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.920
and children in the service of peace.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:05.910
And also, to answer this call of action,

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:09.990
the ECPC was formed and launched at UNICEF

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:14.160
in September, 2013 to join forces

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.780
with the international
community to advance global

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:23.610
and national efforts to prevent
violence and build peace

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.550
through the transformative power

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.880
of early childhood development.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:34.680
Its founding members include
Yale University, UNICEF,

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.740
the Mother and Child
Foundation (ACEV),

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:41.760
Early Years, the organization
for Young Children,

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:46.760
and the United Nations
Alliance of Civilizations.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:51.330
It also brought together many
distinguished organizations

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:56.330
and partners from multiple
sectors, including civil society,

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:00.930
social and mass media,
government officials,

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:05.930
and bilateral agencies as well
as practitioners and academia.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:13.020
The consortium's vision is to
create an inclusive movement

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:17.340
for peace, social justice,
and prevention of violence

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:21.480
through using early childhood
development strategies

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:26.250
and services, not only
to mitigate the immediate

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:29.340
and long-term impact of violence

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.550
and deprivation on children,

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:37.550
but also to build a strong
foundation for peace, resilience,

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:42.180
social justice, and social cohesion.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:46.020
Its goals include to
link emerging knowledge

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.680
from biobehavioral and
environmental sciences

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:53.790
with existing evidence
to increase investment,

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:58.790
advocate for and create local
and sustainable programs

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:04.357
for peace building and reduction
of violence through ECD,

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:10.290
and also to contribute to
the debate on peace building

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:14.040
by focusing on early
childhood development,

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:18.390
engaging governments, civil
societies, communities,

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:23.100
families and children
through science and practice.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:28.100
To advocate and disseminate
information for policy makers,

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:32.463
academics, educators,
parents and caregivers,

00:11:33.373 --> 00:11:37.860
to build this global movement
that values young children

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.700
and families as agents for peace.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:47.300
Also, to promote and advocate
for the research and programs

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:51.240
of the consortium members
that are taking place

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.910
in many areas of the globe

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:58.260
and that contribute to
building peace in societies,

00:11:58.260 --> 00:12:01.590
and you will hear from them afterwards.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:06.590
And most importantly, raise
the voices of families,

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:11.810
parents and children who toil
every day in their cities,

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:17.760
in their villages, in their refugee camps,

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:22.760
to anchor peace in their homes
and in their communities.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:27.093
We want you to join our movement.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:32.910
There is no better time
than now for all of us

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:37.910
to unite our strength, to
erect the building blocks

00:12:37.923 --> 00:12:42.660
of a peaceful future for all children.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:47.660
Let us all accompany families,
let us accompany parents,

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.240
let us accompany caregivers
in raising children of peace,

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.940
and the time is now.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:57.773
Thank you.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.940
- [Jim] Thank you so much, Rima.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.940
It's always a pleasure
